{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492740-tc-opnet-vs-real-internet","id":1492740,"title":"[TC] OpNet vs real Internet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-09T23:02:33-07:00","id":1492740,"title":"[TC] OpNet vs real Internet","content":"<b>OpNet</b> is 'fantastical' new 'network of networks', canonically from <b>Aberrant</b> era onward. ( It's mentioned in <b>Anima</b> and <b>Aeon</b> backstory. ) In Anima there is stated that in 2022 <b><i>Project Utopia</i></b> ( Aeon Society ally Novas / superhumans / ) start the project of replacing classical our modern Internet with OpNet. But <b>what are real advantages of OpNet</b> in the first place? <b>How OpNet works?</b><br /> <br /> Is it working like virtual holographic network from TV show <b>Caprica</b> from 2010, loading you all the senses inputs and sensations from the network? Immersing yourself completely in the events in OpNet? Or does it work differently?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rVbqyBgH_n8\" data-code=\"rVbqyBgH_n8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/rVbqyBgH_n8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T03:15:12-07:00","id":1492747,"title":"","content":"OpNet is just internet, but faster and wireless for everybody. It\u2019s not even virtual reality, at least don\u2019t need to be. It is like the Starlink, but free and needing no special antenna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T10:08:07-07:00","id":1492766,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s built around eufiber. Meaning in 2120, the OpNet <i>still</i> is based on nova core-tech...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T12:27:21-07:00","id":1492770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492740-tc-opnet-vs-real-internet?p=1492766#post1492766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s built around eufiber. Meaning in 2120, the OpNet <i>still</i> is based on nova core-tech...</div> </div> </div> </div>So in <b>Aberrant</b> era they changed normal, rather secure cables network - for bioorganic fiber controlled by Novas that DO NOT give anything better than normal Internet? \ud83e\udd14 It does not have sense! \ud83d\ude2e<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Wolf Wikia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Eufiber</b>, an organic polymer-esque substance was originally secreted from the epidermis of Costa Rican <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nova\" target=\"_blank\">nova</a> Anib\u00e1l Buendia; a synthetic was later created from living colonies of the fibre.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This material has many uses, including <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/OpNet\" target=\"_blank\">OpNet</a> cables and clothing. But living eufiber is greatly prized by novas as the materials' genetic and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Quantum\" target=\"_blank\">quantum</a> pattern conforms to that of the nova wearing it. This means that the eufiber can store a limited amount of quantum energy giving it durability and a natural defence for itself and it's wearer. Also, through this bonding eufiber clothing becomes immune to the nova's powers, making it extremely useful for many novas. It is possible, with careful attuning, for a nova to gain limited contol of a eufiber colony, allowing them to manipulate it as if it was part of their own body.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eufiber\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eufiber</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T13:21:37-07:00","id":1492772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492740-tc-opnet-vs-real-internet?p=1492770#post1492770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So in <b>Aberrant</b> era they changed normal, rather secure cables network - for bioorganic fiber controlled by Novas that DO NOT give anything better than normal Internet? \ud83e\udd14 It does not have sense! \ud83d\ude2e</div> </div> </div> </div><s>Living eufiber can be controlled by a nova, they didn't build the Opnet out of living eufiber. The synthetic eufiber they build the Opnet out of has a basically infinite data transfer capacity with lossless quality.<br /> <br /> If you want a system mechanic way to think about it, living eufiber is nova tech. Anib\u00e1l Buendia has to personally create every inch of living eufiber, but it can do a ton of stuff. Synthetic eufiber is a core tech version just focused on data transfer, and not reliant on Anib\u00e1l Buendia to create it.</s><br /> <br /> Edit: Had 1E Aberrant stuck in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":". 09-10-2022, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T13:48:40-07:00","id":1492774,"title":"","content":"I recall in the 1e Aberrant Players Guide a vampiric eufiber variant. That\u2019s what got me convinced Buendia becomes the Colony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T14:23:57-07:00","id":1492775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492740-tc-opnet-vs-real-internet?p=1492770#post1492770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So in <b>Aberrant</b> era they changed normal, rather secure cables network - for bioorganic fiber controlled by Novas that DO NOT give anything better than normal Internet? \ud83e\udd14 It does not have sense! \ud83d\ude2e<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eufiber\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eufiber</a></div> </div> </div> </div>You're quoting Aberrant 1E. In 2E it is a &quot;complex carbon-silicate nanotube material&quot;, it isn't organic (unless you consider anything made of carbon, like coal or diamonds, to be organic) and it isn't extruded from their body. The benefit is that it is a relatively cheap room temperature superconductor, meaning it can convey electrical signals very quickly and efficiently. Eufiber outperforms fiber optic cable by a huge margin, much like fiber optic cable vastly outperforms copper cable. And since it is core tech, baseline humans are perfectly capably of producing tons of the stuff with no nova involvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T14:42:30-07:00","id":1492776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492740-tc-opnet-vs-real-internet?p=1492772#post1492772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Living eufiber can be controlled by a nova, they didn't build the Opnet out of living eufiber. The synthetic eufiber they build the Opnet out of has a basically infinite data transfer capacity with lossless quality.<br /> <br /> If you want a system mechanic way to think about it, living eufiber is nova tech. Anib\u00e1l Buendia has to personally create every inch of living eufiber, but it can do a ton of stuff. Synthetic eufiber is a core tech version just focused on data transfer, and not reliant on Anib\u00e1l Buendia to create it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s no such thing as \u2018living eufiber\u2019 in TC: Aberrant. It\u2019s all manufactured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T21:56:16-07:00","id":1492782,"title":"","content":"Okay, so... Main difference between real world Internet and OpNet is that Internet is based on fiber optics ( that have data limits, even with 5G technology coming in) - OpNet is based on Eufiber that has near limitless transfer rates? Like we would suddenly jump from 5G tech to 10G tech in transfer with Eufiber?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T22:02:34-07:00","id":1492783,"title":"","content":"I'm just wondering if I can easily ax OpNet project in 2020s, as in my private Continuum variant we did not have (official) Aberrant era with Novas helping humanity - only we jump straight to Aberrant War in 2050s, with few 'Aberrants' showing in 2030s and 2040s.<br /> <br /> Returning to topic - From info you show, I can easily just make Great OpNet building project as whole reconstructions in 2060s, after the Aberrant War - and I will not miss anything, lore and setting-wise. ( Beside positive involvement of Novas in 'new Internet' - but that's the point of my home Timeline.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-11-2022, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T11:35:48-07:00","id":1492815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492740-tc-opnet-vs-real-internet?p=1492783#post1492783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just wondering if I can easily ax OpNet project in 2020s, as in my private Continuum variant we did not have (official) Abberant era with Novas helping humanity - only we jump straight to Aberrant War in 2050s, with few 'Aberrants' showing in 2030s and 2040s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of axing OpNet, just change its origin. TC:Aberrant introduced the process of converting Q-Tech into Nova-tech into Core-Tech; but that process can be translated over to the Super-Science rules found in the core book. The first thing to note is that Q-Tech is a type of Powered Super Science; Nova-Tech is a type of Inspired Super Science; and Core Tech is Advanced Super Science. But even in Aberrant, not everything has to start out as Q-Tech; an inventer <i>could</i> end up devising the specs for a Nova-Tech Device, which is <i>always</i> intended to be usable by anyone, even if only Novas can make it. And like I said, Nova-Tech is a type of Inspired Science; and Talents can <i>also</i> create Inspired Science. <br /> <br /> So just make Eufiber be something that Talents invented. It started out as Inspired Science before getting refined to serve as Advanced Science before becoming so ubiquitous as to be regular science. Or it may have even started out as Advanced Science. Regardless, it can be reimagined as something that doesn't need Novas to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}